 "result_text": "`checkout_github_prs()` now warns and returns without error when `--all`, `--mine` or `--by` match no open PRs. I haven't run the tests or exercised it against GitHub, and flake8 isn't installed here, so I didn't lint the change.\n\nThe change is in `git_machete/client.py`. `__get_valid_pull_requests` used to raise a `MacheteException` for each of those three cases. It now calls `warn(...)` with the same message and returns an empty list. `checkout_github_prs` then returns early on an empty list, before it fetches the remote or touches branches and annotations.\n\nI left the case where you pass explicit PR numbers unchanged. If none of them can be found, it still raises, since that means a PR number you asked for doesn't exist. The issue only talked about \"criteria\", so I read it as covering the three filters. If you want the explicit-numbers case to warn instead, say so.",
